course: dictionary
lesson: 4842
title: Pushing with liquid
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hydraulics is the science and use of liquids, usually oil or water, pushed through pipes to move or lift things. A machine whose hydraulic parts work by liquid pressure is said to use hydraulics.
explain: Why does it work? Liquids cannot be squashed, so when you push a liquid in one place, the push travels along the pipe and comes out at the other end. A small push can lift a very heavy load this way.
explain: Read the context: «A digger's engine drives a pump that pushes oil into pistons, called hydraulics, which move the arm and bucket with huge force.» The clue is pushes oil into pistons: the oil carries the force, so hydraulics means the liquid system that moves the arm.
fact: Hydraulics means using liquid under pressure to move or lift things.
fact: Liquids cannot be squashed, so the push is passed on through the liquid.
fact: Diggers, car brakes, lifts, dentist chairs and aeroplane flaps all use hydraulics.
fact: «Hydraulic lift» and «hydraulic brakes» are phrases you may hear in science and design lessons.
fact: Hydraulics is an uncountable noun and takes a singular verb: say «Hydraulics is useful», not «Hydraulics are useful».
exercise: «A digger's engine drives a pump that pushes oil into pistons.» What does hydraulics mean in this sentence? | The tracks that spread its weight | *The liquid system that moves the digger's arm and bucket | A hole dug in the mud | A kind of digger engine that runs on petrol
exercise: Why can a small push lift a heavy load in a hydraulic lift? | Because the load is secretly very light | Because the pipe gets longer as you push | Because the liquid is hot and floats the load | *Because liquids cannot be squashed, so the push passes along the pipe
exercise: Which of these uses hydraulics? | *A car's brakes | A pencil sharpener | A paper clip | A wooden chair
test: What does hydraulic describe in «hydraulic brakes»? | A part that glows in the dark | A part made of paper | *A part that works by liquid pressure | A part that works by a battery
test: Pick the correct sentence about hydraulics. | The hydraulics of the lift are failing. | The hydraulic of the lift is failing. | The hydraulics of the lift was failings. | *The hydraulics of the lift is failing.
exam: Why does liquid pressure let a small push lift a heavy load? | Pipes make objects weigh less | Heavy loads float on liquids | Liquids are lighter than air | *Liquids cannot be squashed, so the push is passed along the pipe
